LPFQA sits below OpsEval and L-Eval. OpsEval was rejected at avg 5.5 but had a clearly defined evaluation metric (FAE-Score with 0.9185 human correlation) and clean analysis. L-Eval was rejected at avg 6.0 but had careful construction and a principled LLM-judge evaluation. LPFQA has three verified major problems that these papers lack: (1) an internal analytical error directly contradicting the tables, (2) a core framing contradiction where the paper's own experiment refutes its stated purpose, and (3) underspecified evaluation methodology in the main text. These push LPFQA clearly below the OpsEval/L-Eval range. It is substantively better than the Structure-Rich benchmark, which lacked tables and comparisons entirely. I place LPFQA at **3.5** — the analytical error in Section 4.1 and the framing incoherence in Section 4.2.2 are not trivial oversights but represent a quality-control failure significant enough to warrant rejection. The benchmark pipeline and ablation observations have value, but the paper requires substantial revision before it would be credible.

